<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Häme Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tavastehus Castle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Häme Castle is a medieval brick and stone castle in Hämeenlinna, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>. Tradition links its founding to the Swedish expedition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birger-jarl">Birger Jarl</a> to Tavastia around 1249, though the present building dates mainly from the late 13th and 14th centuries. It served as a seat of Swedish royal power in inland Finland and later as a prison, and is now a museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hame-castle.jpg" alt="Häme Castle" width="320" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kanta-Hämeen kuvapankki · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hame_Castle_2019-08.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
